### Phase 0: Prerequisites & Hadoop Environment Setup

#### 1. Update package lists and install Java (OpenJDK 8 or 11) & SSH

Hadoop requires Java. OpenJDK 8 is historically the most stable for Hadoop ecosystems.

```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install -y openjdk-8-jdk wget ssh rsync

```

#### 2. Configure Java Environment Variables

Add Java to your profile so Hadoop can find it:

```bash
echo "export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-8-openjdk-amd64" >> ~/.bashrc
echo "export PATH=\$PATH:\$JAVA_HOME/bin" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
java -version

```

#### 3. Set Up Passwordless SSH for Hadoop

Hadoop uses SSH to manage its daemons.

```bash
ssh-keygen -t rsa -P '' -f ~/.ssh/id_rsa
cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
chmod 0600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
ssh localhost

```

*(Type `yes` if prompted to connect, then type `exit` to return to your shell).*

#### 4. Download and Extract Hadoop (v3.3.6 used as a standard stable release)

```bash
cd ~
wget https://archive.apache.org/dist/hadoop/common/hadoop-3.3.6/hadoop-3.3.6.tar.gz
tar -xzvf hadoop-3.3.6.tar.gz
mv hadoop-3.3.6 hadoop

```

#### 5. Configure Hadoop Environment Variables (`~/.bashrc`)

```bash
echo "export HADOOP_HOME=\$HOME/hadoop" >> ~/.bashrc
echo "export PATH=\$PATH:\$HADOOP_HOME/bin:\$HADOOP_HOME/sbin" >> ~/.bashrc
echo "export HADOOP_CONF_DIR=\$HADOOP_HOME/etc/hadoop" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

```

#### 6. Configure Hadoop XML Files

Update Hadoop's core configuration files to run in pseudo-distributed mode.

* **Update `hadoop-env.sh` to point to Java:**

```bash
echo "export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-8-openjdk-amd64" >> ~/hadoop/etc/hadoop/hadoop-env.sh

```

* **Edit `core-site.xml`:**

```bash
cat << 'EOF' > ~/hadoop/etc/hadoop/core-site.xml
<configuration>
    <property>
        <name>fs.defaultFS</name>
        <value>hdfs://localhost:9000</value>
    </property>
</configuration>
EOF

```

* **Edit `hdfs-site.xml`:**

```bash
cat << 'EOF' > ~/hadoop/etc/hadoop/hdfs-site.xml
<configuration>
    <property>
        <name>dfs.replication</name>
        <value>1</value>
    </property>
</configuration>
EOF

```

* **Edit `mapred-site.xml`:**

```bash
cat << 'EOF' > ~/hadoop/etc/hadoop/mapred-site.xml
<configuration>
    <property>
        <name>mapreduce.framework.name</name>
        <value>yarn</value>
    </property>
</configuration>
EOF

```

* **Edit `yarn-site.xml`:**

```bash
cat << 'EOF' > ~/hadoop/etc/hadoop/yarn-site.xml
<configuration>
    <property>
        <name>yarn.nodemanager.aux-services</name>
        <value>mapreduce_shuffle</value>
    </property>
</configuration>
EOF

```

#### 7. Format the HDFS NameNode

*(Only run this once on a brand-new setup)*

```bash
hdfs namenode -format

```

